# MCP bridge rules

- **Read [`MCP_AGENTS.md`](../../MCP_AGENTS.md) before any Cekura / Gmail /
  Calendar tool call.** It is the operations contract (session roles, env
  checklist, drain SOP, verification).
- The **bot process has no MCP access** — it queues actions to an outbox. Only
  this agent session can fire connectors.

## After a bot WebRTC test → drain the outbox

```bash
cd server
uv run python action_bridge.py --list           # show pending actions
uv run python action_bridge.py --emit            # print connector call specs
# execute each printed MCP call (gmail.create_draft / calendar.create_event)
uv run python action_bridge.py --done <action_id>  # mark fulfilled after success
```

## Connector conventions

- **Email:** only ever send to `OWNER_EMAIL`. Prefer SMTP (real inbox) when
  `GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD` is set; the Gmail MCP only exposes `create_draft`.
- **Calendar:** events are tentative — keep the `[Tentative]` title prefix,
  Graphite `colorId: "8"`, and the `TENTATIVE —` description note. Requires a
  Calendar MCP connected with **write** scope.
- **Cekura:** connect the agent with the **Pipecat** provider; persist runs via
  `persistence.persist_eval_run` (pull with `results_list` first).

## Docs lookups

Prefer the Nia MCP over `WebFetch`/`WebSearch` for indexed repos and docs.
